e function is made up of three triangles. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/f5/f512273895da627c314f00a55bd507d6ae43cd1c6af95d98bd4b475903303e7d.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ f(3) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1)+3 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ f(4) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1)+3+(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**:  Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{2,1,4,3\\}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=1,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186511366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15774" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/80/807e4e931a2872dd6d2a570547b75f68935b3ea761cfaa8cda279a0e194130f9.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[0,5].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3$ and $5$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0,5]$ given that $f(0)=-10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e74c85cc-5f64-54fa-a3ca-fa87e47bcbd2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186511571 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $